2026-10-23T08:02:45.2738991Z 
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2739135Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2739328Z 
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2739410Z Commands:
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2739841Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2740544Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2741384Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2742141Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2743077Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2743775Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2744394Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2745032Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2745701Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2746250Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2746783Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2747276Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-23T08:02:45.2747741Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
